  "name": "CLOSTRIDIUM DIFFICLE TOXIN  A/B AND GDH STOOL",
  "code": "2710",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>.Clostridium difficile Glutamate Dehydrogenase (GDH) is an enzyme produced in large quantities by all toxigenic and nontoxigenic&nbsp;strains, making it an excellent marker for the organism.<br>. Simple and highly sensitive screening assay to make a presumptive diagnosis of Clostridium difficile infection.<br>. Clostridium difficile (C. difficile), a Gram-positive spore bearing anaerobic bacterium is the major aetiological agent of diarrhea and colitis&nbsp;associated with antibioltics.<br>. C. difficile can release two high-molecular-weight toxins, toxin A and toxin B, which are responsible for the clinical manifestations, which&nbsp;range from mild, self-limited watery diarrhea to fulminant pseudomembranous colitis, toxic megacolon, and death.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 99.9535%;\" border=\"1\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 33.3333%;\"><col style=\"width: 33.3333%;\"><col style=\"width: 33.3333%;\"></colgroup>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>GDH</strong></td>\n<td><strong>&nbsp;Toxin A / B</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Interpretation</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>+Ve&nbsp;</td>\n<td>+Ve</td>\n<td>Positive for toxigenic C.difficile</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>+Ve&nbsp;&nbsp;</td>\n<td>-Ve</td>\n<td>PCR- Test required for confirmation</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>1. IDSA/SHEA guidelines recommend testing of patients with &gt; 3 watery, loose, unformed stools for toxigenic c.difficile testing (except in&nbsp;cases of ileus without diarrhoea.)<br>2. Swabs specimen are not appropriate for c.difficile testing.</p>",
